1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,579
This is the complete proposed sputter chamber, assembled with the latest twelve stack gun.

2
00:00:05,579 --> 00:00:07,926
All views use the exported CAD geometry.

3
00:00:07,926 --> 00:00:16,549
The internal space is two hundred millimetres wide, two hundred deep, and three hundred high, giving twelve litres before internal parts and ports.

4
00:00:16,549 --> 00:00:24,820
The assembly contains one hundred and ninety six component instances, including all one hundred and forty one components of the existing gun.

5
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:27,753
These are exact nominal dimensions of this design.

6
00:00:27,753 --> 00:00:33,150
They are not a claim that purchased hardware or fabricated parts have already been verified.

7
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:37,826
The chamber uses ten millimetre walls, roof and floor.

8
00:00:37,826 --> 00:00:40,981
The front sealing frame is sixteen millimetres deep.

9
00:00:40,981 --> 00:00:46,076
The roof blank measures two hundred and twenty by two hundred and twenty six by ten.

10
00:00:46,076 --> 00:00:48,806
The extra depth accommodates the front frame.

11
00:00:48,806 --> 00:00:54,691
The door is two hundred and twenty eight wide, three hundred and sixteen high, and sixteen thick.

12
00:00:54,691 --> 00:00:58,998
Its clear doorway is one hundred and eighty by two hundred and seventy.

13
00:00:58,998 --> 00:01:02,153
The viewport has a seventy millimetre clear opening.

14
00:01:02,153 --> 00:01:06,278
The glass disc is represented as ninety four diameter and six thick.

15
00:01:06,278 --> 00:01:11,556
These thicknesses and seal details still require vacuum structural and supplier review.

16
00:01:11,556 --> 00:01:14,650
The front door gives access without moving the gun.

17
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:21,876
The upper rear K F twenty five port is the gas connection, centred at height two hundred and ten.

18
00:01:21,876 --> 00:01:26,982
The two gauge ports are at height ninety, fifty millimetres to either side of centre.

19
00:01:26,982 --> 00:01:31,547
A V C R adapter can connect the mass flow controller line to the upper port.

20
00:01:31,547 --> 00:01:37,013
The right wall has two spare ports at heights seventy five and two hundred and twenty five.

21
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:39,055
The left wall is completely blank.

22
00:01:39,055 --> 00:01:46,023
The bottom I S O sixty three flange is ninety five millimetres outside diameter, with a sixty three point five bore.

23
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:49,327
Its mating face is forty five below the internal floor.

24
00:01:49,327 --> 00:01:56,775
Gauges, the mass flow controller, and the pump itself are not invented supplier models; the connection interfaces are shown.

25
00:01:58,175 --> 00:02:01,133
The gun axis passes through the centre of the roof.

26
00:02:01,133 --> 00:02:05,077
A welded K F twenty five connection carries the compression adapter.

27
00:02:05,077 --> 00:02:09,079
The existing service tube is twenty five point four outside diameter.

28
00:02:09,079 --> 00:02:18,765
With the target at the highest operating position, the straight section of tube starts at height two hundred and ninety six, four millimetres below the roof underside.

29
00:02:18,765 --> 00:02:24,334
At the lowest position, the tube end still projects twelve point two above the modelled adapter.

30
00:02:24,334 --> 00:02:26,828
This confirms the nominal insertion layout.

31
00:02:26,828 --> 00:02:32,744
However, a standard K F twenty five weld stub or centering ring can have a bore smaller than the tube.

32
00:02:32,744 --> 00:02:36,746
The amber mounting parts identify that unresolved supplier interface.

33
00:02:36,746 --> 00:02:40,400
Their full through bore and sealing geometry must be confirmed.

34
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:47,026
The simple substrate stage is a ninety millimetre diameter plate, six millimetres thick.

35
00:02:47,026 --> 00:02:50,590
Its underside is at height thirty four and its top at forty.

36
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:55,460
Four six millimetre diameter posts support it outside the central pumping opening.

37
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:59,439
The reference substrate is fifty by fifty and one millimetre thick.

38
00:02:59,439 --> 00:03:02,468
Its upper surface is therefore at height forty one.

39
00:03:02,468 --> 00:03:07,813
This surface, rather than the bare stage, is the distance datum used throughout the model.

40
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:14,049
A separate one point five millimetre thick, one hundred and four diameter baffle sits at height eighteen.

41
00:03:14,049 --> 00:03:16,721
It reduces direct deposition toward the pump.

42
00:03:16,721 --> 00:03:19,275
Pumping conductance still needs evaluation.

43
00:03:20,675 --> 00:03:24,121
The gun moves vertically while the substrate remains fixed.

44
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:31,304
The minimum target to substrate gap is seventy five millimetres, putting the target face at height one hundred and sixteen.

45
00:03:31,304 --> 00:03:36,443
The default is one hundred millimetres, putting the target at one hundred and forty one.

46
00:03:36,443 --> 00:03:41,524
The maximum is one hundred and fifty, putting the target at one hundred and ninety one.

47
00:03:41,524 --> 00:03:44,268
That is seventy five millimetres of gun travel.

48
00:03:44,268 --> 00:03:47,831
The animation moves the actual gun solids through this range.

49
00:03:47,831 --> 00:03:51,977
Adjustments are intended with the chamber vented and the gun supported.

50
00:03:51,977 --> 00:03:57,525
These are geometric settings; they do not establish the best deposition distance or uniformity.

51
00:03:58,925 --> 00:04:05,395
The shutter is a single one millimetre sheet with two ninety degree bends, each with a two millimetre inside radius.

52
00:04:05,395 --> 00:04:11,252
Its upper mounting tab lies between heights two hundred and ninety three and two hundred and ninety four.

53
00:04:11,252 --> 00:04:14,375
The lower blade lies between fifty three and fifty four.

54
00:04:14,375 --> 00:04:18,726
The flat midplanes are separated by exactly two hundred and forty millimetres.

55
00:04:18,726 --> 00:04:24,415
The straight vertical portion is two hundred and thirty five long, with the bends completing the drop.

56
00:04:24,415 --> 00:04:31,834
The blade underside is at fifty three and the substrate surface at forty one, so the shutter clearance is exactly twelve millimetres.

57
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:38,025
The blade is fifty six square, giving three millimetres of overhang on each side of the fifty square substrate.

58
00:04:39,425 --> 00:04:43,248
The shutter pivot is sixty five millimetres left of the gun axis.

59
00:04:43,248 --> 00:04:46,601
Turning the top thumb screw rotates the whole bent sheet.

60
00:04:46,601 --> 00:04:49,248
Closed, the blade is centred over the sample.

61
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:52,071
Open, it rotates eighty degrees toward the rear.

62
00:04:52,071 --> 00:04:57,718
The open blade clears the sample edge by about six point six millimetres in the depth direction.

63
00:04:57,718 --> 00:05:01,188
The minimum sampled wall clearance is about two point nine.

64
00:05:01,188 --> 00:05:11,776
We checked eighty one shutter positions, at one degree intervals, against the chamber internals and the gun at seventy five, one hundred, and one hundred and fifty millimetre gaps.

65
00:05:11,776 --> 00:05:15,187
No positive volume interference was found in those checks.

66
00:05:15,187 --> 00:05:20,775
This is nominal CAD clearance; fabrication tolerances and a physical stop still need detailing.

67
00:05:22,175 --> 00:05:29,784
The delivered files contain the complete assembly, open and closed views, individual principal parts, and a developed shutter blank.

68
00:05:29,784 --> 00:05:36,240
The blank uses a neutral axis K factor of zero point four two; the fabricator must adjust it for actual tooling.

69
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:42,293
The shutter screw is represented as one quarter twenty eight, with a six point eight roof clearance hole.

70
00:05:42,293 --> 00:05:48,288
McMaster head details and the rotating O ring seal are reference envelopes, not a qualified feedthrough.

71
00:05:48,288 --> 00:05:55,955
The gun mounting bore, door and viewport seals, glass rating, and chamber pressure strength must also be verified before fabrication.

72
00:05:55,955 --> 00:06:04,025
The model now establishes the complete arrangement and its nominal dimensions, while keeping those remaining engineering decisions explicit.
